{"base_rate":0.30381471389645776,"brier":0.29077029972752044,"bss":-0.3747268049107966,"bss_hi":-0.2057145731777322,"bss_lo":-0.5457774486184149,"chart":{"base":[324.6,351.1],"fp":[191.0,34.0],"lead":"62,279.1 272,274.8 482,274.5 692,253.3","note":{"base":"skill -0.37 — higher than 4% of cities","fp":"low end -2pp, high end +41pp","lead":"day-1 error 0.8 °C — better than 91% of cities","rel":"promised 12% → rained 7%; promised 99% → rained 66%"},"rel":"135.6,436.6 319,395 479.9,368.2 605.5,299.4 684.8,182.8"},"country":"PR","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.3119073569482289,"ess":444.2414837084238,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Ponce</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Ponce rain forecast is cannot beat its own climatology, though 8 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>66%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(4%), there is still roughly a <b>6%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 734 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nPONCE 3.2 NNE, 3.5 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score -0.37, ranked 207 of\n216 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(204&ndash;211) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>4%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>65</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>18%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>82</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>33%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'><b>16%</b></td><td class='num'>79</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>61%</td><td class='num'><b>20%</b></td><td class='num'>70</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>72%</td><td class='num'><b>25%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>82%</td><td class='num'><b>36%</b></td><td class='num'>81</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>91%</td><td class='num'><b>42%</b></td><td class='num'>72</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>66%</b></td><td class='num'>151</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">8 of 9 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Ponce</b> <span class=\"muted\">Puerto Rico</span></p>\n  <div class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag bad\">Cannot beat climatology</span><details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What does this label mean?\" title=\"What does this label mean?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>Compared with a simple guess: saying &ldquo;30% chance of rain&rdquo; every day, because it rains here on 30% of days.</p><p>The forecast did worse than that guess.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details>\n    <span class=\"muted\">8 points off by more than chance</span></div>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score<details class=\"ginfo\"><summary aria-label=\"What is the skill score?\" title=\"What is the skill score?\">?</summary><div class=\"ginfo-pop\" role=\"note\"><p>How much better the forecast is than that simple guess. 0 means no better, 1 means perfect, below 0 means worse. Day-ahead rain forecasts usually score 0.3 to 0.5.</p><p><a href=\"#bss\">How the skill score works</a></p></div></details></dt><dd>-0.37</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>204&ndash;211\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 216</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>734 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Ponce &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Ponce\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\"