 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"71.452\" cy=\"359.6\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 18%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 82 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"121.4609756097561\" cy=\"355.3658536585366\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 33%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"174.3973134328358\" cy=\"322.23880597014926\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 48%&amp;#10;It rained 16% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 79 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"226.2172151898734\" cy=\"322.1012658227848\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 61%&amp;#10;It rained 20% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 70 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"274.6985714285714\" cy=\"309.2\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 72%&amp;#10;It rained 25% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"311.7176119402985\" cy=\"289.64179104477614\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 82%&amp;#10;It rained 36% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 81 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"348.5859259259259\" cy=\"251.679012345679\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 91%&amp;#10;It rained 42% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 72 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"380.0416666666667\" cy=\"230.33333333333331\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 66% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 151 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"407.9676821192053\" cy=\"143.35099337748343\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(30%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Ponce the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>winter</b> (-0.22) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (-0.77).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>178</td><td class='num'>22%</td><td class='num'>-0.770</td><td class='num'>38.5%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>216</td><td class='num'>32%</td><td class='num'>-0.399</td><td class='num'>32.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>174</td><td class='num'>40%</td><td class='num'>-0.276</td><td class='num'>29.2%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>166</td><td class='num'>27%</td><td class='num'>-0.221</td><td class='num'>23.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":18.01031,"lon":-66.62398,"n":734,"n_cities":216,"name":"Ponce","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.1,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.038000000000000006,"n":65,"obs":0.06153846153846154,"sig":false},{"hi":0.25599999999999995,"lo":0.1,"mean":0.17926829268292685,"n":82,"obs":0.07317073170731707,"sig":true},{"hi":0.41,"lo":0.25599999999999995,"mean":0.3288059701492537,"n":67,"obs":0.16417910447761194,"sig":true},{"hi":0.57,"lo":0.41,"mean":0.4751898734177215,"n":79,"obs":0.16455696202531644,"sig":true},{"hi":0.67,"lo":0.57,"mean":0.6121428571428572,"n":70,"obs":0.2,"sig":true},{"hi":0.78,"lo":0.67,"mean":0.7167164179104478,"n":67,"obs":0.2537313432835821,"sig":true},{"hi":0.87,"lo":0.78,"mean":0.8208641975308641,"n":81,"obs":0.35802469135802467,"sig":true},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.87,"mean":0.9097222222222222,"n":72,"obs":0.4166666666666667,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9886092715231787,"n":151,"obs":0.6556291390728477,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":3.5,"provisional":false,"rank":207,"rank_hi":211.0,"rank_lo":204.0,"reliability":0.12022821990778053,"resolution":0.04330128248840061,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"ponce","station":"PONCE 3.2 NNE","timezone":"America/Puerto_Rico"}